    "mainmenu.subtitle": "Café Nocturne — a night café by the station",
    "menu.black_coffee.desc": "Strong enough to stand a spoon in.",
    "menu.black_coffee.name": "Black, Lida-style",
    "menu.bryndzove_pirohy.desc": "With bacon and sour cream. Natália won't hear a word against them.",
    "menu.bryndzove_pirohy.name": "Bryndza pierogi",
    "menu.cappuccino.desc": "Milk foam and five minutes of peace.",
    "menu.cappuccino.name": "Cappuccino",
    "menu.chai.desc": "Cinnamon, cardamom and a scent that lasts till morning.",
    "menu.chai.name": "Spiced chai",
    "menu.chlebicek.desc": "Ham, egg, gherkin. Works even without electricity.",
    "menu.chlebicek.name": "Open sandwich",
    "menu.garlic_soup.desc": "With cheese and croutons. Chases off the cold and the night shift.",
    "menu.garlic_soup.name": "Garlic soup",
    "menu.grandma_kulajda.desc": "Dill, mushrooms, a poached egg — and the secret ingredient from Lida's book.",
    "menu.grandma_kulajda.name": "Grandma's kulajda",
    "menu.hot_chocolate.desc": "Thick as the night. Sometimes paid for with a song.",
    "menu.hot_chocolate.name": "Hot chocolate",
    "menu.kolac.desc": "Quark and poppy seed, still warm from the oven.",
    "menu.kolac.name": "Kolach",
    "menu.lemon_tea.desc": "Two sugars, if you're the gentleman by the window.",
    "menu.lemon_tea.name": "Tea with lemon",
    "menu.medovnik.desc": "Twelve layers and patience.",
    "menu.medovnik.name": "Honey cake",
    "menu.night_train.desc": "A double espresso, garlic toast and a kolach for the road. For those travelling on.",
    "menu.night_train.name": "The Night Train",
    "menu.oat_flat_white.desc": "For drone pilots and anyone who thinks the cow is asleep.",
    "menu.oat_flat_white.name": "Oat flat white",
    "menu.svarak.desc": "Cloves, orange and warm hands.",
    "menu.svarak.name": "Mulled wine",
    "menu.topinka.desc": "Fried in lard, the proper way. A Mirek classic.",
    "menu.topinka.name": "Garlic toast",
    "menu.varenyky.desc": "With potato and fried onion, the way Oleh's mum makes them.",
    "menu.varenyky.name": "Varenyky",
    "note.note_01.text": "Don't switch off the light in the window before six. It isn't superstition. It's a promise.",
    "note.note_01.where": "Under the register",
    "note.note_02.text": "Mirek: black, toast. Hana: cappuccino, quickly! Vera: tea, kolach, and don't argue. The gentleman by the window: tea with lemon, two sugars. Don't take his money.",
    "note.note_02.where": "In the cupboard behind the counter, once everything is spotless",
    "note.note_03.text": "When the lights go out, people tell the truth. Keep the candles dry.",
    "note.note_03.where": "In the fuse box",
    "note.note_04.text": "Those who heal get served without queueing.",
    "note.note_04.where": "Under the armchair cushion",
    "note.note_05.text": "Kulajda: dill, mushrooms, a poached egg and a spoonful of vinegar from the bottle J. gave me. Vera knows more than she says.",
    "note.note_05.where": "In the recipe book Vera kept",
    "note.note_06.text": "He always pays with coins that no longer exist. I don't take his money.",
    "note.note_06.where": "Among the coins from the window table",
    "note.note_07.text": "M. looks at me as if he were guilty. I forgave him long ago — whatever it is.",
    "note.note_07.where": "On the back of an old bill",
    "note.note_08.text": "3:33. I reached the platform two minutes late. All my life, two minutes.",
    "note.note_08.where": "Inside Radek's old timetable",
    "note.note_09.text": "If he comes again, tell him I waited. Not for my sake. For the light's.",
    "note.note_09.where": "Inside the repaired radio",
    "note.note_10.text": "A café isn't its walls. It's the people who come. Don't sell them.",
    "note.note_10.where": "Behind the photo on the wall, once the café has a good name",
    "regular.filip.bio": "Filip Kadlec, 22, technical college student. All night by the socket with his laptop, a black coffee every hour. Pays little, stays long.",
    "regular.filip.line.0a": "Is there a socket somewhere? Please. I'm at two per cent.",
    "regular.filip.line.0b": "One more black coffee. Entropy is rising.",
    "regular.filip.line.1a": "The guys from my year asked where you can study at night. I told them. Sorry.",
    "regular.filip.line.2a": "…",
    "regular.filip.line.3a": "Resit on Friday. Keep your fingers crossed.",
    "regular.filip.line.4a": "A B! A B!",
    "regular.filip.name": "Filip",
    "regular.guest_333.bio": "Arrives at exactly 3:33, leaves at 3:50. Tea with lemon, two sugars. Pays with coins that are no longer money.",
    "regular.guest_333.line.0a": "…",
    "regular.guest_333.line.1a": "You keep them. I don't need them anymore.",
    "regular.guest_333.line.2a": "Still lit. That's good.",
    "regular.guest_333.line.3a": "I left once. I never managed to come back.",
    "regular.guest_333.line.4a": "Tonight it will stop. I can feel it.",
    "regular.guest_333.name": "The man in the grey coat",
    "regular.guest_anwar.ambient.busy": "Lively tonight. I'll keep quiet, then.",
    "regular.guest_anwar.ambient.coffee": "Good flat white. Don't tell the oats they're not milk.",
    "regular.guest_anwar.ambient.fog": "Can't even see the tracks. Just the light from your window.",
    "regular.guest_anwar.ambient.late": "Two in the morning is the most honest hour.",
    "regular.guest_anwar.ambient.midnight": "Midnight already? The cursor doesn't care.",
    "regular.guest_anwar.ambient.quiet": "A quiet night. The best kind.",
    "regular.guest_anwar.ambient.rain": "I like it when the rain does the talking.",
    "regular.guest_anwar.ambient.train": "Every train sounds like it's going somewhere better.",
    "regular.guest_anwar.bio": "A quiet guest, late twenties. Sits by the socket, works on his laptop, orders an oat flat white and leaves around two.",
    "regular.guest_anwar.name": "Anwar",
    "regular.hana.bio": "Hana Janoušková, 38, night nurse at the district hospital. Break at two, soup after the shift. Always in a hurry.",
    "regular.hana.line.0a": "Cappuccino, please. Quick, I've got six minutes.",
    "regular.hana.line.0b": "…",
    "regular.hana.line.1a": "Three admissions and one birth tonight. A girl. Her name's Lida, would you believe it?",
    "regular.hana.line.2a": "I'll just close my eyes for a second…",
    "regular.hana.line.3a": "Dresden wrote again. They pay twice as much. And here… here I know everyone.",
    "regular.hana.line.4a": "I've decided. For real this time.",
    "regular.hana.name": "Hana",
    "regular.lori.bio": "Loreta \"Lori\" Benešová, 27, street musician. Plays on the platform in the rain. Pays with a song.",
    "regular.lori.line.0a": "It's raining. Holešovice's platform has the best acoustics in Prague.",
    "regular.lori.line.1a": "This one's for the crossword lady. She frowns the prettiest.",
    "regular.lori.line.2a": "A stage! A real one! Well, almost.",
    "regular.lori.line.3a": "I'm playing Friday. Tell everyone.",
    "regular.lori.name": "Lori",
    "regular.mirek.bio": "Miroslav Dvořák, 80. The last taxi driver in Holešovice who still drives himself. Black coffee and toast every night. Pays exact, never tips.",
    "regular.mirek.line.0a": "This place used to be full till morning. In Lida's day.",
    "regular.mirek.line.0b": "Robots drive better. But they don't know where the best toast is.",
    "regular.mirek.line.1a": "Pour it like you would for Lida. She knew… never mind.",
    "regular.mirek.line.2a": "That board has small letters. It's not my eyes.",
    "regular.mirek.line.3a": "I walked here tonight. It's nicer than I thought.",
    "regular.mirek.line.4a": "Twenty grams. And a whole life.",
    "regular.mirek.line.5a": "A few more nights. Then I have to decide.",
    "regular.mirek.name": "Mirek",
    "regular.radek.bio": "Radek Macek, 52, station dispatcher. Twice a night \"for five minutes\", at one and half past four. Coffee to go, now.",
    "regular.radek.line.0a": "Three minutes. The train won't wait. Well, it would, but the computer won't.",
    "regular.radek.line.1a": "I'll let you know if the express is running late. For your stock's sake.",
    "regular.radek.line.2a": "Last shift. Strange feeling.",
    "regular.radek.line.3a": "Do you know about the express that got stuck in the snowdrifts in '85? Sit down.",
    "regular.radek.name": "Radek",
    "regular.vera.bio": "Vera Soukupová, 83, widow, Lida's classmate and rival. Does crosswords from half past midnight to three. Strict about dirty tables.",
    "regular.vera.line.0a": "Lida wouldn't have done it like that.",
    "regular.vera.line.0b": "Eight letters, \"one who waits\". Hm.",
    "regular.vera.line.1a": "Come here, young people. \"Night bird, five letters.\" No, it isn't Mirek.",
    "regular.vera.line.2a": "That table is clean. Lida would have been… well, satisfied.",
    "regular.vera.line.3a": "Another bowl of kulajda. For old times' sake.",
    "regular.vera.line.4a": "Tomorrow I'm bringing friends. Brace yourself.",
    "regular.vera.name": "Mrs Vera",
    "sandbox.character.calm.desc": "2–4 events a night, the occasional big one. A bad night is followed by a calm one.",
    "sandbox.character.calm.name": "Calm",
    "sandbox.character.changeable.desc": "3–5 events a night. Calm one night, chaos the next.",
    "sandbox.character.changeable.name": "Changeable",
    "sandbox.character.chaotic.desc": "5–8 events a night, no breathers. For hardened night owls.",
    "sandbox.character.chaotic.name": "Chaotic",
    "sandbox.character.quiet.desc": "1–3 events a night, hardly any big ones. For winding down.",
    "sandbox.character.quiet.name": "Quiet",
    "sandbox.character.stormy.desc": "4–6 events a night; trouble comes in pairs.",
    "sandbox.character.stormy.name": "Stormy",
    "sandbox.institution.college": "College and dorms",
    "sandbox.institution.culture_house": "Culture house",
    "sandbox.institution.depot": "Logistics depot",
    "sandbox.institution.drone_hub": "Drone hub",
    "sandbox.institution.highway": "Motorway rest stop",
    "sandbox.institution.hospital": "Hospital",
    "sandbox.institution.police": "Police and fire station",
    "sandbox.institution.taxi_rank": "Taxi rank",
    "scene.act2.01": "A week. The cups have stopped rattling in your hands.",
    "scene.act2.02": "The town has started to talk: the window by the station is lit again.",
    "scene.act2.03": "More applicants have seen your schedule. Three new people want night shifts.",
    "scene.act2.04": "Who on earth wants night shifts?",
    "scene.act2.05": "People who can't sleep. People saving up. People running from something. The usual.",
    "scene.act4_storm.01": "A storm comes over the hills from Frýdlant.",
    "scene.act4_storm.02": "At 22:30 the station lights go out, then the street lamps, then all of Holešovice.",
    "scene.act4_storm.03": "Only one window is still lit. Grandma's lamp runs on a battery older than you.",
    "scene.act4_storm.04": "So that's why, Grandma.",
    "scene.act4_storm.05": "The door opens and closes, again and again. Everyone who is awake is coming.",
    "scene.answer.01": "Dawn. The man in the grey coat is still by the window. Your grandmother's letter lies open in front of him.",
    "scene.answer.02": "He reads it twice. The second time, his lips move.",
    "scene.answer.03": "\"I'll wait. The light in the window will be on.\"",
    "scene.answer.04": "So she waited.",
    "scene.answer.05": "For sixty years I thought nobody had. For sixty years I came to check.",
    "scene.answer.06": "Thank you, Mirek. Better late than in the rain.",
    "scene.answer.07": "Forgive me.",
    "scene.answer.08": "I already have. She did first — read the bottom.",
    "scene.answer.09": "Thank you for keeping it on.",
    "scene.answer.10": "He walks out onto the platform. The train takes him without a sound.",
    "scene.answer.11": "For one second the board shows: Rn 333 — ODJEL. Then it shows nothing at all.",
    "scene.answer.12": "That morning, for the first time in sixty years, Mirek sleeps until noon.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_24.01": "It's almost done. The game.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_24.02": "I've been writing it here, you know. The rain, the lamp in the window, the trains. Thank you for the atmosphere.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_24.03": "We didn't do anything special.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_24.04": "That's exactly what I needed.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_24.05": "He closes the laptop, leaves the exact amount by his cup and buttons up his coat.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_24.06": "The last train. Good night — and keep the light on.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_9.01": "The man by the socket looks up from his laptop, as if surprised that anyone noticed him.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_9.02": "Sorry, I got a bit lost in it. I'm making a small game. About a night café in the rain.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_9.03": "Nothing explodes in it. People just come in, drink something warm and go on their way.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_9.04": "I keep wondering if anyone would ever play something that quiet.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_9.05": "Some people need exactly that.",
    "scene.anwar_talk_9.06": "Maybe. …Another flat white, then. For research.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.01": "The new sign arrives on the 05:20 from Frýdlant: NONSTOP 24, in letters that never sleep.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.02": "Debt settled, contract signed. Congratulations, manager. From now on, we're open round the clock.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.03": "The lamp comes out of the window to make room for a promo screen. Nobody will have to wait for it anymore. It will simply always be on.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.04": "I'm sorry. The numbers didn't add up. The lease ends this morning.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.05": "The last night of Café Nocturne. Not a game over. Just the end of a long shift.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.06": "But they come. One by one, before dawn, without being asked.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.07": "Give me that box. You're packing the cups wrong. Lida packed them wrong too.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.08": "I'll walk you to the train. Walk. Jana took my keys.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.09": "Open something of your own. Anywhere. I'll find it — I always find the coffee.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.10": "I'll write you a song. A sad one, but with a good chorus.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.11": "I'll send you my address once I've got my own flat. With a socket by the table. In your honour.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.12": "The 06:12 to Beroun. I checked. It's on time. Of course it is, I'm not the one running it anymore.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.13": "The regulars come for a last coffee. A few words, a few handshakes. Holešovice at night isn't a place for big goodbyes.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.14": "You take Grandma's recipe book, the photo from the wall, and the key that was under the mat.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.15": "Sorry, Grandma. I kept it on as long as I could.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.16": "To whoever keeps the light: the light isn't a building. Take it with you.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.17": "The 06:12 leaves for Beroun. Through the window, the station grows small, then the town, then the fog.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.18": "Somewhere down the line — Frýdlant, Ejpovice, Děčín — there are towns that stay awake at night. And people who would come, if a window were lit.",
    "scene.ending_last_train.19": "Thirty nights. Long enough to learn how.",
    "scene.ending_light.01": "06:00. The thirtieth night is over.",
    "scene.ending_light.02": "The last payment arrived at 05:59. Ninety thousand. I… I'll draw up a new lease.",
    "scene.ending_light.03": "Not all of it came in on time. But the town has sent me forty-two messages about this café. Forty-two. I'll extend the lease — on condition that you make them stop.",
    "scene.ending_light.04": "And that light in the window… keep it. It suits the station.",
    "scene.ending_light.05": "Jana drives me now. Slowly. She drives like her mother.",
    "scene.ending_light.06": "I told Dresden no. I'll be back at two — keep the armchair free.",
    "scene.ending_light.07": "I've brought three friends. They complain even more than I do. You'll love them.",
    "scene.ending_light.08": "Next semester I'm taking the corner table again. Reserved. Under the socket.",
    "scene.ending_light.09": "Retired men need somewhere to tell their stories. You've been warned.",
    "scene.ending_light.10": "Fridays. My guitar. Your hot chocolate. Deal?",
    "scene.ending_light.11": "Lida would have said it's all wrong. And then she'd have sat down and stayed.",
    "scene.ending_light.12": "Somebody puts the kettle on. Somebody else starts washing cups without being asked. At six in the morning the café is full, and nobody wants to go home.",
    "scene.ending_light.13": "The café is quiet. A few cups, a few chairs. The light is on — and for now, there's nobody to wait for. But the night is long, and the neighbourhood is small.",
    "scene.ending_light.14": "You walk to the window. Outside, Holešovice is waking up: the first self-driving tram, a drone carrying bread, a fox on its way home.",
    "scene.ending_light.15": "A café isn't its walls. It's the people who come. Don't sell them.",
    "scene.ending_light.16": "I won't, Grandma.",
    "scene.ending_light.17": "At exactly six, you switch off the light in the window. For the first time as the owner. And tomorrow at ten in the evening, you'll switch it on again.",
    "scene.filip_cake.01": "I passed! Thermodynamics, a B. I brought a cake. It's a bit squashed, I came on the drone bus.",
    "scene.filip_cake.02": "Thanks for never kicking me off the table with the socket. Half my degree happened on it.",
    "scene.filip_exam.01": "Filip hasn't even opened his laptop tonight. He's staring into a cold coffee.",
    "scene.filip_exam.02": "I failed. Thermodynamics, third attempt. Dad says I should go work at the drone depot like a normal person.",
    "scene.filip_exam.03": "Send someone kind to sit with him",
    "scene.filip_exam.04": "Bring him a fresh coffee on the house",
    "scene.filip_exam.05": "Don't interfere",
    "scene.filip_exam.06": "…One more attempt. Fine. But if I fail again, I'm putting this café in my excuse note.",
    "scene.final_night.01": "The thirtieth night. The last payment is due at six.",
    "scene.final_night.02": "Tonight's schedule: everyone. Nobody asked for a swap. Nobody asked for time off.",
    "scene.final_night.03": "Let's keep the light on, then.",
    "scene.franchise_decision.01": "Well? The contract is in your Shiftella inbox. One tap.",
    "scene.franchise_decision.02": "On the wall, Grandma's photo. In the window, the lamp. Outside, the town is asleep — except for the people who come here.",
    "scene.franchise_decision.03": "Sign. The debt disappears, the café becomes NONSTOP 24.",
    "scene.franchise_decision.04": "Refuse. Café Nocturne stays Café Nocturne.",
    "scene.franchise_decision.05": "Excellent! Our team arrives tomorrow with the new sign. You'll love the lighting.",
    "scene.franchise_decision.06": "…I'm sure.",
    "scene.franchise_decision.07": "Pity. Sentiment is expensive, you know.",
    "scene.franchise_decision.08": "So is coffee. We manage.",
    "scene.franchise_visit.01": "Day seventeen. A silver car with no driver parks where Mirek usually does.",
    "scene.franchise_visit.02": "Petr Šindelář, NONSTOP 24. Lovely place. Terrible opening hours.",
    "scene.franchise_visit.03": "Here's our offer: we pay off the entire debt. You stay on as manager. Open 24/7, our menu, our sign. Everything modern.",
    "scene.franchise_visit.04": "And the light in the window?",
    "scene.franchise_visit.05": "With us, the lights never go out! That's rather the point.",
    "scene.franchise_visit.06": "Think it over until the twenty-second night. Unlike our shops, our offers don't stay open forever.",
    "scene.franchise_visit.07": "Calendar: \"NONSTOP 24 — decision\" added to night 22.",
    "scene.guest333_first.01": "03:33. The second hand on the wall clock stops.",
    "scene.guest333_first.02": "The radio hisses softly, as if somebody far away were tuning it.",
    "scene.guest333_first.03": "A man in a grey coat is sitting by the window. Nobody heard the door.",
    "scene.guest333_first.04": "Tea with lemon, please. Two sugars.",
    "scene.guest333_first.05": "He drinks slowly, watching the platform. Then he's gone — and on the table lie three coins that haven't been money for longer than you've been alive.",
    "scene.guest333_first.06": "Czechoslovak crowns. 1978.",
    "scene.guest333_first.07": "The clock ticks again. 03:34.",
    "scene.guest333_question.01": "The clock has stopped again. For the first time, the man in the grey coat looks up from the platform.",
    "scene.guest333_question.02": "Is she still waiting?",
    "scene.guest333_question.03": "\"Yes. The light is still on.\"",
    "scene.guest333_question.04": "\"I don't know.\"",
    "scene.guest333_question.05": "\"She's gone. This autumn.\"",
    "scene.guest333_question.06": "Good. Then I'll keep coming.",
    "scene.guest333_question.07": "Nobody knows. That's the worst part of waiting.",
    "scene.guest333_question.08": "…Gone. And the light is still on.",
    "scene.guest333_question.09": "Then someone is keeping it for her.",
    "scene.guest333_ticket.01": "Tonight he left no coins. On the table lies a ticket: Rn 333, Praha-Holešovice 3:33, 14 November 1979. A return.",
    "scene.guest333_ticket.02": "The return half was never used.",
    "scene.hana_asleep.01": "02:20. Hana has fallen asleep over her cappuccino, still in her scrubs.",
    "scene.hana_asleep.02": "Her phone lights up: \"Break ends 02:30.\" And again: \"Offer from the Dresden clinic — please reply.\"",
    "scene.hana_asleep.03": "Wake her gently — her break is ending",
    "scene.hana_asleep.04": "Cover her with a blanket and let her sleep ten more minutes",
    "scene.hana_asleep.05": "Move her to the armchair under the lamp, the quiet corner",
    "scene.hana_asleep.06": "Thanks… I'd have slept through the whole ward.",
    "scene.hana_asleep.07": "I haven't slept like that in a month. …Don't tell the head nurse.",
    "scene.hana_decision.01": "I've decided. About Dresden.",
    "scene.hana_decision.02": "I'm staying. Dresden pays better. Prague has a chair under a lamp where somebody lets me sleep.",
    "scene.hana_decision.03": "I'm going. It's a good job. …Thanks for all the coffee. You were always quick.",
    "scene.last_333.01": "For the first time in sixty years, a train stops at 3:33. Its windows are warm and empty.",
    "scene.last_333.02": "That one's mine. Tea, please, before I go. Two sugars.",
    "scene.last_333.03": "Place Lida's letter beside his cup",
    "scene.last_333.04": "Keep the letter in your pocket",
    "scene.last_333.05": "Jindra.",
    "scene.last_333.06": "Mirek. You got old.",
    "scene.last_333.07": "You didn't.",
    "scene.last_333.08": "Mirek puts the letter on the table. With both hands, as if it were heavy.",
    "scene.last_333.09": "He doesn't open it yet. He just rests his palm on it.",
    "scene.last_333.10": "I'll wait for the morning. I'd like to see what the town looks like with the light on.",
    "scene.last_333.11": "Nothing tonight either. That's all right. I'm used to it.",
    "scene.last_333.12": "The train takes him away without a sound.",
    "scene.lori_evening.01": "Rain on the windows. Every chair taken. Lori tunes her guitar on the little stage.",
    "scene.lori_evening.02": "This one's for the café that let me in out of the rain.",
    "scene.lori_evening.03": "For three songs, nobody orders anything. Then everybody orders everything.",
    "scene.lori_platform.01": "On the empty platform, under the dripping shelter, someone is playing guitar. Out of tune, but the singing is beautiful.",
    "scene.lori_platform.02": "Don't worry, I'm not playing for the trains. They don't tip.",
    "scene.lori_platform.03": "Do you have… hot chocolate? I can't pay. I can play, though.",
    "scene.lori_platform.04": "Come in, it's warm in here",
    "scene.lori_platform.05": "Sorry, not tonight",
    "scene.lori_platform.06": "A song for a chocolate. Fair trade.",
    "scene.lori_platform.07": "Sure. I get it. Have a good night.",
    "scene.mirek_confession.01": "There's something I have to tell you. I've carried it for sixty years. It weighs about twenty grams.",
    "scene.mirek_confession.02": "From his inside pocket he takes an envelope. Yellowed. Sealed. In Lida's hand: \"For Jindra.\"",
    "scene.mirek_confession.03": "November '79. Jindra was leaving on the night train, the Rn 333. They'd quarrelled. She wrote this and asked me to run it to him on the platform.",
    "scene.mirek_confession.04": "I was twenty and crazy about her. I stood in the rain and watched the train leave. And I kept it.",
    "scene.mirek_confession.05": "He never came back. She never stopped waiting. And I came here every night for coffee and never said a word.",
    "scene.mirek_confession.06": "Every night. For sixty years.",
    "scene.mirek_confession.07": "Black, like Lida made it. Yes. Every night.",
    "scene.mirek_curb.01": "A crunch outside. Mirek's old car has kissed the kerb by the entrance.",
    "scene.mirek_curb.02": "The kerb moved. They move them at night, you know. The city council.",
    "scene.mirek_curb.03": "He squints at the menu board for a long time. Too long.",
    "scene.mirek_curb.04": "The letters on that board have got smaller since Lida's day.",
    "scene.mirek_curb.05": "Make the menu font bigger (−300 CZK)",
    "scene.mirek_curb.06": "Read the menu out to him",
    "scene.mirek_curb.07": "Say nothing",
    "scene.mirek_curb.08": "Black. As always. At least something doesn't change.",
    "scene.mirek_first.01": "The door bell. An old man in a cap shakes the rain off his shoulders. A taxi driver, judging by the keys.",
    "scene.mirek_first.02": "So the light's on again. I thought I was seeing ghosts.",
    "scene.mirek_first.03": "Black coffee. Like Lida made it — strong enough to stand a spoon in.",
    "scene.mirek_first.04": "I'll try. I'm her grandchild.",
    "scene.mirek_first.05": "…You've got her eyes. Lord. Well. Coffee, then. And toast, if the stove's still alive.",
    "scene.mirek_first.06": "Take the order, make the coffee at the machine, and take the money at the register.",
    "scene.mirek_letter.01": "Tell me what to do with it. I've had sixty years and I still don't know.",
    "scene.mirek_letter.02": "\"Give it to me. I'll keep it safe.\"",
    "scene.mirek_letter.03": "\"Keep it. It's yours to carry.\"",
    "scene.mirek_letter.04": "\"Burn it. Let it rest.\"",
    "scene.mirek_letter.05": "\"Give it to him yourself. On the thirtieth night, at 3:33.\"",
    "scene.mirek_letter.06": "Myself? …If I give it to him myself — will he see me?",
    "scene.mirek_letter.07": "He sees everyone who's waiting.",
    "scene.mirek_letter.08": "The envelope curls up in the stove. Mirek watches until nothing is left.",
    "scene.mirek_letter.09": "Light. That's all it ever was.",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.01": "Brakes. A shout. Mirek's car stops a hand's breadth from a nurse crossing to the hospital.",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.02": "Nobody is hurt. Mirek sits at the bar with shaking hands and doesn't touch his coffee.",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.03": "I didn't see her. The lights, the rain… I didn't see her.",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.04": "Don't look at me like that. The taxi is all I've got left. The robots took the rest of the town.",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.05": "Ask him for his car keys",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.06": "Call his daughter Jana",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.07": "Say nothing",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.08": "…Lida would have done the same. Only she'd have shouted first.",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.09": "Dad? I'm on my way. Don't you dare get behind the wheel.",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.10": "My own daughter. Like I'm a schoolboy.",
    "scene.mirek_pedestrian.11": "Mirek finishes, pays the exact amount and drives off. His tail lights smear in the rain.",
    "scene.opening.01": "Praha-Holešovice, autumn 2039. A big city that, at night, shrinks to one station, one river and a great deal of fog.",
    "scene.opening.02": "Regional train Os 2141 from Adamov has arrived at platform one. Thank you for travelling at night.",
    "scene.opening.03": "The train hums away into the dark on its own — it hasn't needed a driver for years. On the platform: one suitcase and one person. You.",
    "scene.opening.04": "Last I remember, that counter came up to my nose.",
    "scene.opening.05": "Beside the station, one dark window. Above it, a holo sign with a cracked letter: CAFÉ NOCTURNE — kavárna u nádraží.",
    "scene.opening.06": "In your pocket, a letter from the notary. And one more, handwritten. On the envelope: \"To whoever keeps the light.\"",
    "scene.opening.07": "If you're reading this, the coffee machine has outlived me. Be nice to it. It bites.",
    "scene.opening.08": "The key is under the mat. Of course it is. Nobody in Holešovice steals mats.",
    "scene.opening.09": "I won't lie to you: there are debts. Ninety thousand. The landlord is giving you thirty nights.",
    "scene.opening.10": "We open at ten at night and close at six in the morning. And the light in the window stays on until six. Always.",
    "scene.opening.11": "Why, I can't put in a letter. You'll find out. Your Lida.",
    "scene.opening.12": "Dust. Chairs on the tables. On the wall, a photo of Grandma — laughing at someone outside the frame.",
    "scene.opening.13": "All right, Grandma. Thirty nights.",
    "scene.opening.14": "You switch on the lamp in the window. Somewhere beyond the tracks, a fox stops and looks.",
    "scene.payment_1.01": "Morning. The first payment leaves with the 06:12 to Beroun.",
    "scene.payment_1.02": "Payment received. Honestly? I didn't expect it.",
    "scene.payment_1.03": "The payment didn't arrive in full. I won't make a scene. Yet.",
    "scene.payment_1.04": "One more thing: the lease ends after the thirtieth night. I'll only extend it if the debt is paid. Nothing personal. Arithmetic.",
    "scene.payment_1.05": "Then we'll do arithmetic.",
    "scene.payment_2.01": "Second payment's in. I'm starting to get used to this. That's dangerous.",
    "scene.payment_2.02": "Money's short again. And yet the café seems full. I don't understand it.",
    "scene.payment_2.03": "Halfway to the thirtieth night.",
    "scene.payment_3.01": "Third payment. You know people write to me about you? Normally people only write to me about mould.",
    "scene.payment_3.02": "The third payment doesn't add up again. At least people write that your soup is good.",
    "scene.payment_4.01": "Fourth payment. One left — thirty thousand. I'm keeping my fingers crossed. Don't tell anyone.",
    "scene.payment_4.02": "The fourth payment is missing. One night left. Show me a miracle, or at least a calculator.",
    "scene.radek_last_shift.01": "Last shift. From tomorrow, the station runs itself.",
    "scene.radek_last_shift.02": "I brought you something. The old timetable from the dispatcher's office. 1979. I was supposed to shred it.",
    "scene.radek_last_shift.03": "Look at the last line. Somebody wrote next to it in pencil: \"two minutes\".",
    "scene.radek_news.01": "Black, to go. I've got four minutes.",
    "scene.radek_news.02": "They're automating the station. In two weeks I'm the last night dispatcher at Holešovice — after that, just the computer and the fog.",
    "scene.radek_news.03": "Funny thing. The old timetable on the wall still has the Rn 333. Arrival 3:33. Cancelled in '79, and nobody ever took it down.",
    "scene.radek_news.04": "Rn 333?",
    "scene.radek_news.05": "These days, a night train from nowhere to nowhere. Ask the old-timers. Or better don't.",
    "scene.vera_first.01": "So you're the grandchild. Lida's.",
    "scene.vera_first.02": "Tea with lemon. And wipe that table. Lida would never have left it like that.",
    "scene.vera_first.03": "I'm doing my best.",
    "scene.vera_first.04": "Everyone does their best. Lida's best was better.",
    "scene.vera_first.05": "She opens a crossword and doesn't look up again. But she stays until three.",
    "scene.vera_jindrich.01": "First snow. Lida loved it. Sit down, I'll tell you about Jindra.",
    "scene.vera_jindrich.02": "He fixed radios. Tall, shy, a terrible dancer. She chose him over half the town. Over Mirek, too.",
    "scene.vera_jindrich.03": "The night he left for work in Ostrava, they quarrelled. Over something silly — money and pride. She said she'd write.",
    "scene.vera_jindrich.04": "He waited for a letter that never came. She waited for a man who never came back. And I watched them both, too proud to say anything either.",
    "scene.vera_jindrich.05": "That's why I came here and complained about the tables. Somebody had to keep her company.",
    "scene.vera_recipe.01": "Here. Lida's recipe book. She gave it to me to \"keep away from the grease\". In 1994.",
    "scene.vera_recipe.02": "Her kulajda. Dill, mushrooms, a poached egg and something she never told me. Maybe she wrote it down.",
    "scene.vera_recipe.03": "I know more than I say, child. But not tonight.",
    "scene.vera_tears.01": "…This is it. Exactly hers.",
    "scene.vera_tears.02": "We fought about everything. Boys, exams, who had nicer hair. I always lost. I never minded as much as I claimed.",
    "scene.vera_tears.03": "Vera cries quietly into the soup. Then she asks for more bread.",
    "staff.barista.bio": "Bára dropped out of university in Prague and hasn't told her parents. Her coffee is better than her thesis was.",
    "staff.barista.dislikes": "Silence, washing up",
    "staff.barista.likes": "Music in the hall, chatting with guests",
    "staff.barista.role": "Night barista",
    "staff.cashier.bio": "Ivana works nights while her daughter sleeps at the neighbour's. One phone call can upend a whole shift.",
    "staff.cashier.dislikes": "Lateness, chaos",
    "staff.cashier.likes": "Precision, being praised",
    "staff.cashier.role": "Register & floor",
    "staff.cook.bio": "Mr Holub cooked for twenty years in the glassworks canteen. He knew Lida and grumbles that \"it was different in her day\".",
    "staff.cook.dislikes": "Rushing, people touching his things",
    "staff.cook.likes": "An orderly kitchen, his own knife",
    "staff.cook.role": "Cook",
    "staff.porter.bio": "Kuba used to haul crates at a warehouse. He's kind and drops everything. Secretly, he's learning to bake.",
    "staff.porter.dislikes": "Loud arguments",
    "staff.porter.likes": "Animals (cats!), food",
    "staff.porter.role": "Helper & cleaning",
    "staff.quiet_one.bio": "Ema hears the horns of trains that aren't in the timetable. She's the only one who notices the clock stopping at 3:33.",
    "staff.quiet_one.dislikes": "Crowds, harsh light",
    "staff.quiet_one.likes": "Rain, the quiet hours between two and four",
    "staff.quiet_one.role": "All-rounder",
    "staff.server.bio": "Natália came from Košice for a week and stayed. She carries four plates at once and remembers every name.",
    "staff.server.dislikes": "Sticky floors",
    "staff.server.likes": "Clean tables, rainy nights",
    "staff.server.role": "Server",
    "staff.sound_tech.bio": "Oleh was a sound engineer in Lviv. He's been here \"temporarily\" for two years now. He can fix an old radio.",
    "staff.sound_tech.dislikes": "Cheap coffee",
    "staff.sound_tech.likes": "Old records, the radio",
    "staff.sound_tech.role": "Bar & floor",
    "story.act.1.title": "Act I — The Keys",
    "story.act.2.title": "Act II — The Regulars",
    "story.act.3.title": "Act III — The Offer",
    "story.act.4.title": "Act IV — The Last Train",
    "story.hint.app": "Shiftella has shift swaps, time off, announcements and the morning digest.",
    "story.hint.armchair": "An armchair with a floor lamp beside it makes a quiet corner.",
    "story.hint.build": "In Build (B) you can add tables, lamps and plants. Money is taken right away; Ctrl+Z undoes.",
    "story.hint.candles": "Without power, only cold food can be sold. Candles cheer the guests up.",
    "story.hint.downpour": "Downpour! More guests are coming in — put someone on cleaning.",
    "story.hint.farewell": "The last nights. Every regular comes to close their story.",
    "story.hint.first_order": "Click the guest at the counter, then the coffee machine. For now, the staff is you.",
    "story.hint.hire": "You can hire during the day. Open Crew (C) and pick a candidate.",
    "story.hint.inspection": "The inspection checks dirt. Under 30 % earns praise, over 60 % a fine.",
    "story.hint.lori_night": "Lori is here. Tonight she plays for everyone.",
    "story.hint.morning": "At six the café closes. In the morning you'll see the night's summary.",
    "story.hint.new_staff": "More people are applying for night shifts. Take a look at the candidates.",
    "story.hint.payment": "The 90,000 CZK debt is paid on nights 7, 14, 21, 28 and 30. The overview is in the Shiftella app.",
    "story.hint.priorities": "In Priorities (P) you decide who does what first. 1 is most important.",
    "story.hint.regulars": "Regulars have their own hours and favourites. Serve them quickly and they'll open up.",
    "story.hint.rush": "Rush! Give Bar and Serving top priority.",
    "story.hint.schedule": "The shift schedule lives in the Shiftella app (T). Click a cell to change the draft, then Publish.",
    "story.hint.special": "New special: the Night Train. For those travelling on.",
    "story.hint.window_light": "The lamp in the window must be on at 3:33 too.",
    "story.line.04_mirek": "There's always a strange silence here around three. Lida said it was nothing.",
    "story.line.06_filip": "Good evening… is there Wi-Fi? Or at least a socket?",
    "story.line.07_cook": "In Lida's day the payments were made on Sundays too. In the morning. With swearing.",
    "story.line.11_ema": "Do you hear that? A train. There's none on the board.",
    "story.line.16_kuba": "A cat would like it here. If there were one. Just saying.",
    "story.line.18_filip": "Don't ask. Please.",
    "story.line.22_vera": "Lida would have been proud. Don't tell her… well, don't tell anyone.",
    "story.line.22_vera_sold": "So now it just shines here. It doesn't wait.",
    "story.line.29_radek": "You sleep terribly in retirement. So here I am.",
    "story.night.01.hint": "The key is under the mat. Light the window and make the first coffee.",
    "story.night.01.title": "Arrival",
    "story.night.02.hint": "Hire someone and build your first schedule.",
    "story.night.02.title": "The first colleague",
    "story.night.03.hint": "At two, someone arrives who has no time to wait.",
    "story.night.03.title": "Rain and a nurse",
    "story.night.04.hint": "Keep the window lit. All night.",
    "story.night.04.title": "3:33",
    "story.night.05.hint": "After midnight, someone who knew Lida will come. Keep the tables clean.",
    "story.night.05.title": "The crossword lady",
    "story.night.06.hint": "Saturday. Around eleven, the concert at the culture house ends.",
    "story.night.06.title": "After the concert",
    "story.night.07.hint": "At six in the morning, 15,000 CZK is due. Count carefully.",
    "story.night.07.title": "The first payment",
    "story.night.08.hint": "New people are applying. And Mirek is parking oddly tonight.",
    "story.night.08.title": "The kerb",
    "story.night.09.hint": "At one, the dispatcher stops by. He has four minutes.",
    "story.night.09.title": "The last dispatcher",
    "story.night.10.hint": "Have candles ready. Just in case.",
    "story.night.10.title": "Darkness",
    "story.night.11.hint": "It's raining. Someone is playing on the platform.",
    "story.night.11.title": "A song on the platform",
    "story.night.12.hint": "An armchair and a lamp might come in handy tonight.",
    "story.night.12.title": "The quiet corner",
    "story.night.13.hint": "The health inspector comes around half past eleven. Make it shine.",
    "story.night.13.title": "Inspection",
    "story.night.14.hint": "The second payment. And Vera is bringing something tonight.",
    "story.night.14.title": "The recipe book",
    "story.night.15.hint": "Fog. At 3:33, someone will ask you something.",
    "story.night.15.title": "The question",
    "story.night.16.hint": "Nobody will come. Time for cleaning — and for the people who work here.",
    "story.night.16.title": "An empty night",
    "story.night.17.hint": "A visitor from the NONSTOP 24 chain arrives. Listen.",
    "story.night.17.title": "NONSTOP 24",
    "story.night.18.hint": "Filip hasn't opened his laptop tonight.",
    "story.night.18.title": "The resit",
    "story.night.19.hint": "It's going to pour. Twice the guests — and twice the mess.",
    "story.night.19.title": "Downpour",
    "story.night.20.hint": "Mirek will be late tonight. Stay near the door.",
    "story.night.20.title": "A hand's breadth",
    "story.night.21.hint": "Another payment at six. Someone wants a holiday.",
    "story.night.21.title": "The third payment",
    "story.night.22.hint": "Tonight decides whose sign hangs over the door.",
    "story.night.22.title": "The decision",
    "story.night.23.hint": "Radek is working his last shift.",
    "story.night.23.title": "The timetable",
    "story.night.24.hint": "It's raining. If Lori has a stage, tonight is hers.",
    "story.night.24.title": "Lori's evening",
    "story.night.25.hint": "A storm is coming. Keep the window lit.",
    "story.night.25.title": "The storm",
    "story.night.26.hint": "Hana has made up her mind.",
    "story.night.26.title": "Dresden",
    "story.night.27.hint": "It's snowing. Vera wants to tell a story.",
    "story.night.27.title": "First snow",
    "story.night.28.hint": "The fourth payment. And Mirek has a question.",
    "story.night.28.title": "The letter",
    "story.night.29.hint": "Every regular comes tonight to close their story.",
    "story.night.29.title": "Farewells",
    "story.night.30.hint": "The last night. 30,000 CZK at six. At 3:33, keep the window lit.",
    "story.night.30.title": "The last train",
    "train.announce.arrival": "Train {train} from {from} to {to} is arriving at {time} at platform {platform}.",
    "train.announce.delay": "Train {train} from {from} to {to}, due at {time} at platform {platform}, is delayed. Thank you for your patience.",
    "train.en_471.name": "EN 471 — night express Cheb → Frýdlant",
    "train.nex_9002.name": "Nex 9002 — self-driving freight",
    "train.os_2141.name": "Os 2141 — regional from Adamov",
    "train.r_815.name": "R 815 — fast train Frýdlant → Beroun",
    "train.rn_333.name": "Rn 333 — not in any timetable since 1979",
    "trait.anxious.desc": "Afraid of mistakes — and makes them when the queue grows. Careful at the register, though.",
    "trait.anxious.name": "Anxious",
    "trait.calm.desc": "Power cut? Then we light candles. Bad news only half reaches them.",
    "trait.calm.name": "Calm",
    "trait.chatterbox.desc": "Knows everything about every guest. Guests love it; work slows down when it's quiet.",
    "trait.chatterbox.name": "Chatterbox",
    "trait.clumsy.desc": "The hands have other plans. Every now and then, a plate goes clink.",
    "trait.clumsy.name": "Clumsy",
    "trait.early_bird.desc": "Unstoppable until midnight, foggy after two.",
    "trait.early_bird.name": "Early Bird",
    "trait.grumpy.desc": "Grumbles, but knows the trade. Patient guests like the \"real character\".",
    "trait.grumpy.name": "Grumpy",
    "trait.hard_worker.desc": "Won't leave until it's done. Skips breaks when there's a queue — and pays for it later.",
    "trait.hard_worker.name": "Hard Worker",
    "trait.kind.desc": "Comforts guests and colleagues alike. Everyone nearby feels a little better.",
    "trait.kind.name": "Kind",
    "trait.lazy.desc": "Breaks are sacred. Works slower, but doesn't tire as fast either.",
    "trait.lazy.name": "Lazy",
    "trait.light_sleeper.desc": "Hears what others don't. Notices the 3:33 guest and sometimes senses what's coming.",
    "trait.light_sleeper.name": "Light Sleeper",
    "trait.loner.desc": "Works best when nobody's around. A crowd of colleagues wears down the mood.",
    "trait.loner.name": "Loner",
    "trait.music_lover.desc": "Works to the beat. Blooms with music, wilts in silence — and turns the radio on unasked.",
    "trait.music_lover.name": "Music Lover",
    "trait.neat.desc": "Can't walk past a stain. Cleans faster, and without being asked.",
    "trait.neat.name": "Neat",
    "trait.night_owl.desc": "Comes alive at night, sleeps like a log by day. Tires much more slowly after midnight.",
    "trait.night_owl.name": "Night Owl",
    "trait.perfectionist.desc": "Slow, but perfect. Better tips — and a bad mood when things get dirty.",
    "trait.perfectionist.name": "Perfectionist",
    "trait.romantic.desc": "Falls in love with colleagues and with the rain. Rainy nights lift the mood.",
    "trait.romantic.name": "Romantic",
    "tutorial.app.body": "Open Shiftella (T). In the schedule, click a cell to change a shift, then Publish — the night follows the published schedule. Requests, messages and the board live there too.",
    "tutorial.app.title": "The schedule in Shiftella",
    "tutorial.build.body": "Build (B): pick a piece, click in the café. R rotates, X demolishes, Ctrl+Z undoes. Lamps, plants and a rug make guests happier.",
    "tutorial.build.title": "Make the hall cosy (optional)",
    "tutorial.crew.body": "Open Crew (C). Candidates are at the bottom — a barista helps from the very first night. One click on Hire.",
    "tutorial.crew.title": "Hire your first helper",
    "tutorial.enjoy.body": "That's all. F1 or the \"?\" in the dock opens How to play. May the window stay lit until morning.",
    "tutorial.enjoy.title": "Enjoy the night",
    "tutorial.events.body": "News and little happenings pop up bottom right. Some have buttons — choose one, or wait and the night picks for you. They wait while paused.",
    "tutorial.events.title": "Events",
    "tutorial.guests.body": "Hover a guest to see what they want and how long they'll wait. Regulars have their own stories — click one, and when they have something to say, Talk appears.",
    "tutorial.guests.title": "Guests",
    "tutorial.money.body": "Top right: the till, reputation stars and the debt. In the morning you get a summary of the night; during the day you'll see when the next payment is due.",
    "tutorial.money.title": "Money and reputation",
    "tutorial.priorities.body": "Priorities (P): rows are people, columns are jobs. 1 = does it first, empty = never. Click to raise, right-click to lower. Give everyone one clear 1.",
    "tutorial.priorities.title": "Who does what",
    "tutorial.staff.body": "People pick up work by their priorities. In Crew (C) you'll see their needs — energy, hunger, mood. Tired people take a break on their own.",
    "tutorial.staff.title": "Your crew works on its own",
    "tutorial.start.body": "Whenever you're ready, press Start the night (or Enter). Light the window and make the first coffee.",
    "tutorial.start.title": "Open the doors",
    "tutorial.time.body": "Space pauses, 1/2/3 change the speed. The bar under the clock is the night until 06:00; the little marks are trains — each brings a small rush.",
    "tutorial.time.title": "Time at your pace",
    "tutorial.welcome.body": "Days are for planning: people, the schedule, furniture. At night, 22:00–06:00, the café runs — you keep an eye on it. A few tips, then it's all yours.",
    "tutorial.welcome.title": "Welcome to Café Nocturne",
    "tutorial.welcome_sandbox.body": "A few cards show how things work: days for planning, nights 22:00–06:00 for running the café. You can skip the tour at any time.",
    "tutorial.welcome_sandbox.title": "A quick tour?",
    "ui.app.approve": "Approve",
